!CHECK 221651.40 | 221646.10 00 | line 1 B,JTRYLG -- JTRYLG is printed p.194 line 44's label at 221646.00; a B shows bit 32 only, so 0o10 is the branch code
!CHECK 221652.00 | 221201.01 B0 | line 2 LVE,0,RV4 -- the byte is B0 and NOT the 80 a 400 dpi read gives (glyph call 2); RV4 is the landed 221201.0 and .01 is the LVE index encoding for register 0
!CHECK 221652.40 | 221727.01 30 | line 3 SV,0,J WKOM+1.0 -- JWKOM is THIS page's line 43 at 221726.00, so +1.0 is 221727.00 and the row is a REAL address check of a label defined fifteen cards later.  PRINTED WITH A BLANK IN THE NAME; see departure (A)
!CHECK 221653.00 | 221726.00 10 | line 4 LX,$0,JWKOM -- the same label unindexed; printed p.194 line 44 prints the identical card against JERGK and the same byte 10
!CHECK 221653.40 | 221512.40 80 | line 5 SIC,KKRET -- a SIC reads every bit, so this row CHECKS the landed KKRET at 221512.40; printed p.194 line 45 prints the identical word
!CHECK 221654.00 | 221505.10 00 | line 6 B,KIOREJ -- landed 221505.0; printed p.194 line 46 prints the identical word
!CHECK 221654.40 | 221655.43 01 | line 7 LVI,$1,$+1.0 -- $ is this row's own 221654.40 so $+1.0 is 221655.40; .43 is 0o40 (bit 32) OR 2J+1 = 3 for J=1.  SELF-CHECKING: it depends on nothing but this page's counter.  Byte 01, not the C1 the drum prints (glyph call 1)
!CHECK 221655.00 | 221525.10 00 | line 8 B,JSEOPT -- JSEOPT is printed p.192 line 27's label at 221525.00
!CHECK 221655.40 | 000000.30 00 | line 9 NOP
!CHECK 221656.00 | 000000.30 00 | line 10 NOP
!CHECK 221656.40 | 221660.50 00 | line 11 B,JWTERR -- JWTERR is THIS page's line 14 at 221660.40: 0o40 OR the branch code 0o10 = 0o50, so this pins the label
!CHECK 221657.00 | 221730.00 80 000021.06 A0 | line 12 TI,3,JPREVX,$1 -NORMAL RETURN -- JPREVX is THIS page's line 45 at 221730.00, so the first half is a real address check; $1's cell is word 0o21.  THE BYTE IS A0: the second operand carries no index, so I2 = 0 (glyph call 3)
!CHECK 221660.00 | 221660.10 00 | line 13 JWRITX B,$ -- $ is this row's own location, so the word is self-checking; printed p.189 line 8 SYNs JWRITX here through a SIC, BIT-EXACT, which is what makes this deck's origin CHECKED
!CHECK 221660.40 | 221645.06 48 | line 14 JWTERR CB,$3,JBACKT -TRY AGAIN -- 0o06 is 2J = 6 for J=3 with bit 32 clear, so JBACKT is at 221645.00, which is printed p.194 line 42's label
!CHECK 221661.00 | 221663.10 00 | line 15 B,JNEUT -- JNEUT is THIS page's line 19 at 221663.00
!CHECK 221661.40 | 221520.40 80 | line 16 JERRD SIC,JBSPX -BACKSPACE THE TAPE -- a SIC reads every bit, so this CHECKS the landed JBSPX at 221520.40 (printed p.192 line 8's label)
!CHECK 221662.00 | 221514.10 00 | line 17 B,JBSPE -- landed 221514.0
!CHECK 221662.40 | 221636.06 48 | line 18 CB,$3,JRDLAB -- 0o06 is 2J for J=3 with bit 32 clear, so JRDLAB is at 221636.00 on printed p.194; the same byte 48 as line 14
!CHECK 221663.00 | 221614.00 80 | line 19 JNEUT SIC,JNEWT -TRY TO GET A NEW TAPE -- a SIC, so this CHECKS the landed JNEWT at 221614.00 to the bit
!CHECK 221663.40 | 221541.10 00 | line 20 B,JNEWTE -- JNEWTE is printed p.192 line 51's label at 221541.00
!CHECK 221664.00 | 221634.50 00 | line 21 B,JUNRL -TRY AGAIN -- 0o50 is 0o40 OR 0o10, so JUNRL is at 221634.40 on printed p.194.  Location carries the trailing asterisk
!CHECK 221664.40 | 000010.44 3C | line 22 JBDLAB LV,$2,SCREEL($12) -IS IT A SCRATCH TAPE -- SCREEL is the landed displacement 8.32 = 0o10.40, and .44 is that OR 2J = 4 for J=2.  THE BYTE IS 3C and not 30: the low nibble is the operand's index $12 (glyph call 4)
!CHECK 221665.00 | 000000.42 82 036017.06 70 | line 23 LF(BU,30),.34($2),30 -CURRENT REEL NAME -- ".34" is a BARE DECIMAL bit offset, 34 decimal = 0o42, which is the workflow's bare-literal rule put to work; the second half carries length 0o36 = 30 and the offset 30
!CHECK 221666.00 | 000000.40 8B 221667.74 02 | line 24 BB,SOWNER($11),$+1.32 -- BB's first operand is a 24-BIT BIT ADDRESS, so the landed SOWNER at 0.32 prints .40 bit-exactly; $ is 221666.00 so $+1.32 is 221667.40, printing 0o40 OR the BB code 0o34 = 0o74.  Low nibble B is index $11
!CHECK 221667.00 | 221663.34 C0 | line 25 BZRZ,JNEUT -IF NOT A SCRATCH TAPE -- JNEUT is THIS page's line 19 at 221663.00 and 0o34 is the BZ-reset branch code; byte C0 is genuine on both glyphs (glyph call 5)
!CHECK 221667.40 | 000006.00 8C 036000.12 F0 | line 26 SF(BU,30),SSCRPM($12) -AND IN UAT -- SSCRPM is the landed displacement 6.0 and the operation writes NO dds of its own, so the length 0o36 = 30 in the second half comes from the dds this deck carries on the SYN; low nibble C is index $12
!CHECK 221670.40 | 221644.50 00 | line 27 B,JRWRIT -GO TO REWRITE LABEL -- the landed JRWRIT at 221644.40: 0o40 OR 0o10
!CHECK 221721.00 | 000000.00 8E 000137.15 00 | line 38 JUNLDK CTL(SEOP),0.0($14),(8)137.0 -UNLOAD COMMAND -- 8E's low nibble is index $14; .15 is the CTL(SEOP) code; 0o137 is the unload control code written in STRAP's ADDRESS form, which the assembler keeps word-granular
!CHECK 221722.00 | 000000.00 8E 221723.11 00 | line 39 JRDLK RD(SEOP),0.0($14),$+1.0 -READ LABEL COMMAND -- $ is 221722.00 so $+1.0 is 221723.00, which is line 40's control word; .11 is the RD(SEOP) code
!CHECK 221723.00 | 221724.00+ 000 000001 000000 | line 40 CW,$+1.0,1.0 -- the chain address is $+1.0 = 221724.00, which is JLABIN on line 41, so the row pins the next label; the count "1.0" is a BIT address and converts to one word
!CHECK 221724.00 | 000000.00+ 000 000000 000000 | line 41 JLABIN XW,0 -LABEL SLOT -- an empty index word, the slot the label is read into
!CHECK 221725.00 | 000000.00 8E 000056.15 00 | line 42 JERGK CTL(SEOP),0.0($14),(8)56.0 -- the same shape as line 38 with control code 0o56 (erase long gap); printed p.194 line 44 branches here through LX,$0,JERGK
!CHECK 221726.00 | 000000.00 8E 221727.13 00 | line 43 JWKOM W(SEOP),0.0($14),$+1.0 -WRITE LABEL COMMAND -- $+1.0 is 221727.00, line 44's control word; .13 is the W(SEOP) code.  Location carries the trailing asterisk
!CHECK 221727.00 | 000006.00+ 000 000001 000000 | line 44 CW,SSCRPM($12),1.0 -- the landed SSCRPM at 6.0 as an 18-bit WORD address, count one word, flags 000.  PRINTED WITH AN INDEX, which strap_asm's CW refuses; a control word has no index field and the compiled word is identical -- departure (B).  Location carries the LEADING asterisk
